{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules","id":133915,"title":"Sin-eater History and Background Expansion (\"Fluff Houserules\")","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-12T09:56:34-07:00","id":133915,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Sin-eater History and Background Expansion (\"Fluff Houserules\")","content":"<a href=\"https://www.mediafire.com/?g777mige3tw1rpg\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://www.mediafire.com/?g777mige3tw1rpg\" target=\"_blank\">he PDF</a><br /> <br /> Much as I <b>love</b> <i>Geist</i>, it has a lot of problems. Some--like the way the Krewe Channel completely remakes your Geist and you believe it was always secretly Santa Claus, as one person put it--are handwaved or ignored, the same way that Predator's Taint is often ignored. Other parts, unfortunately, are less about too much information and more about completely missing information. Sin-eaters have little in common with each other beyond being Sin-eaters, and they have no real antagonists to speak of. A lot of players don't even know about Abmortals because they've only been given a few pages. This is compared to groups like VII and the Seers, who have quite a bit of information given about them.<br /> <br /> Since other than the Ready Made Player Characters and <i>Geist</i>'s as of yet unspoiled entry in <i>Dark Eras</i> there's little in the foreseeable future for the Bound, I want to try to expand on them myself. <i>Geist</i>, despite being a rather unique kind of character to the <i>World of Darkness</i> and an interesting one at that, gets a lot of flack, and many of the complaints are valid. So let's hear what <b><i>you</i></b> don't like about <i>Geist</i>. Whether you're a fan and love the game, or you hate it and dislike the presentation, I want to hear what we the players can do to make <i>Geist</i> better.<br /> <br /> I don't plan on creating a whole new thing, though I do have plans for providing houserules to make the game work with the <i>God-Machine Chronicle</i> rules updates. This won't be a <i>Rum and Bones: The Kerberoi Chronicle</i> or anything, but if all goes well, it will reinvigorate interest in *Geist* and encourage Onyx Path to make more supplements for it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Here's a quick list of things I want to address</b></span><br /> <br /> \u25cf Plasm generation (one plasm a scene from ofrendas and one per week for a Haunt is ridiculous)<br /> <br /> \u25cf De-emphasizing krewe channels and Tier 3 krewes (the Tier system from Hunter feels very unnecessary here, and goes against much of the rest of the fluff, but it gets a long series of rules and merits anyway)<br /> <br /> \u25cf More about Abmortals, and why Sin-eaters would come into conflict with them.<br /> <br /> \u25cf More reasons for Sin-eaters to go into the Underworld beyond it being cool (even though it totally is)<br /> <br /> \u25cf Meaningful emphasis on Archetypes as diverse groups and their importance in Plasm generation<br /> <br /> \u25cf Meaningful emphasis on Thresholds as more than just starting Key and fluff of the Sixth Sense<br /> <br /> \u25cf Giving krewes a reason to be together<br /> <br /> \u25cf Fleshing out the Sin-eater antagonists, in particular Abmortals, the Sacrosanct, Cthonians, the Vacant, and the Church of the Unified Spirit, a cult that worships the Bound as the perfect expression of humanity.<br /> <br /> \u25cf Power level fix concerning Manifestations (every sin-eater gets at least +3 to their starting Manifestation/Key combo as is, and then can get Mementos)<br /> <br /> \u25cf Discussion of Sin-eater culture around the world, including Asia, Africa, the Middle East, and the pre-Colombian Americas.<br /> <br /> \u25cf Various bits and bobs concerning the Twilight Network, Gravedigger's Cant/Old Tongue, and the Horsemen, adding to the culture of Death and giving it something more concrete.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><i><b>Any suggestions are more than welcome!</b></i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 05-12-2014, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T14:11:55-07:00","id":134337,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules#post133915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some--like the way the Krewe Channel completely remakes your Geist and you believe it was always secretly Santa Claus, as one person put it--are handwaved or ignored, the same way that Predator's Taint is often ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, too, ignore blatant falsehoods and misrepresentations of the way the game has things work. I'm having some difficulty understanding how this is a <i>change.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Here's a quick list of things I want to address</b></span><br /> <br /> \u25cf Plasm generation (one plasm a scene from ofrendas and one per week for a Haunt is ridiculous) </div> </div> </div>Haunts have generated plasm nightly since the 1.1 updates, which have been out for nearly two years now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u25cf De-emphasizing krewe channels and Tier 3 krewes (the Tier system from Hunter feels very unnecessary here, and goes against much of the rest of the fluff, but it gets a long series of rules and merits anyway) </div> </div> </div>I'd greatly prefer <i>not</i> to remove the game's primary means of throwing in weird mythologia, if it's all the same to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u25cf Power level fix concerning Manifestations (every sin-eater gets at least +3 to their starting Manifestation/Key combo as is, and then can get Mementos) </div> </div> </div>The +3 bonus is from your keystone, which is a memento. Memento bonuses explicitly don't stack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T15:21:32-07:00","id":134444,"title":"","content":"I'll just note Mortal Remains gives some history on Sin-Eaters. Not a great deal, but a glimpse of what they were up to during the later Victorian Era and Second World War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T15:57:35-07:00","id":134537,"title":"","content":"I kind of hate that <i>Mortal Remains</i> had more about Sin-eater history than <i>Geist</i>. Much as I love Hunter, I bought Mortal Remains for the Sin-eater stuff. The fact that it included a generic monster template that lets me run a Hunter-rules-only &quot;crossover&quot; game is just an incredibly awesome bonus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=134337#post134337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some thoughts:<br /> I, too, ignore blatant falsehoods and misrepresentations of the way the game has things work. I'm having some difficulty understanding how this is a <i>change.</i><br /> I'd greatly prefer <i>not</i> to remove the game's primary means of throwing in weird mythologia, if it's all the same to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're fine feeling that way, but in my experience most people don't like the krewe channel and the way that it drastically rearranges your Geist. Having your Geist turn into something new and reveal some great truth that you believe because it comes from your Psyche no matter how ludicrous it is, that's something most people don't really care for and don't include in their games. <br /> Likewise, unless the game is specifically about Tier 3 krewes, that part of the book is likely to be ignored.<br /> <br /> That said, I actually <i>wasn't</i> aware that Haunts had been fixed in 1.1, and I hadn't ever caught on that Memento bonuses don't stack (which might explain why my Sin-eaters were so powerful). And it does make me wonder what the point of other Momentos are if they don't actually stack. But regardless every Sin-eater is still going to get +3 to their power set thanks to their Keystone. While number of dice isn't really a good metric of power, it's a bit hard to fail when you're rolling <i><b>twelve</b></i> of them between Attribute + Skill + Manifestation + Keystone.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not like I'm forcing anyone to use this fluff. You can still have a krewe channel that alters your Geist and gives you a great and terrible revelation. It's just that as described the average Krewe Channel feels to me something more fitting for the Sacrosanct than your average Sin-eater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T16:26:20-07:00","id":134617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=134537#post134537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of hate that <i>Mortal Remains</i> had more about Sin-eater history than <i>Geist</i>. Much as I love Hunter, I bought Mortal Remains for the Sin-eater stuff. The fact that it included a generic monster template that lets me run a Hunter-rules-only &quot;crossover&quot; game is just an incredibly awesome bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, my goal was to make it as useful as possible to to both Hunter and Geist players. Of course, where push comes to shove Hunter got the win, because Hunter book, but having it be useful to Geist players including having some appropriate history was the goal.<br /> <br /> As for the rulebook, from what I am told the biggest thing was space. They had one book for everything, and the lack of a concise timeline was bowing to that. Sin-Eaters are very much caught up in the now. Part of that was necessity, part because it was different than everyone else, even ones like Hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T16:29:20-07:00","id":134619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=134537#post134537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're fine feeling that way, but in my experience most people don't like the krewe channel and the way that it drastically rearranges your Geist. Having your Geist turn into something new and reveal some great truth that you believe because it comes from your Psyche no matter how ludicrous it is, that's something most people don't really care for and don't include in their games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you didn't understand my meaning:<br /> <br /> <i><b>That isn't how the game concept actually works and by giving credence to the notion that it does you are either deliberately lying or at the very least thoughtlessly propagating misinformation.</b></i><br /> <br /> That's not a matter of feelings so much as basic epistemic ethics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise, unless the game is specifically about Tier 3 krewes, that part of the book is likely to be ignored. </div> </div> </div>&quot;That part&quot; here being &quot;one sidebar, baseline krewe benefits, and maybe three pages total of minor references to how they're all but entirely gone (unless the rumors are true or you make a new one) spread throughout a three-hundred page corebook.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am literally in the process of rereading the corebook at this very moment. The krewe creation section was the section I started rereading <i>today.</i> I know what I'm talking about when I say that the book does not give overmuch attention to global conspiracies of Sin-Eaters as a concept, contrary to your implicit assertion that it does so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it's not like I'm forcing anyone to use this fluff. You can still have a krewe channel that alters your Geist and gives you a great and terrible revelation. It's just that as described the average Krewe Channel feels to me something more fitting for the Sacrosanct than your average Sin-eater. </div> </div> </div>Again, my problem is not that this is proposing a change. My problem is that you are claiming the book says things it does not say, whether deliberately or inadvertently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T16:29:58-07:00","id":134620,"title":"","content":"Memento bonuses are for other keys<br /> <br /> Now, if only there was a way fans of Geist could pool our money in advance for further Geist books, to guarantee that they won't be made at a loss...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T18:12:43-07:00","id":134728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=134617#post134617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, my goal was to make it as useful as possible to to both Hunter and Geist players. Of course, where push comes to shove Hunter got the win, because Hunter book, but having it be useful to Geist players including having some appropriate history was the goal.<br /> <br /> As for the rulebook, from what I am told the biggest thing was space. They had one book for everything, and the lack of a concise timeline was bowing to that. Sin-Eaters are very much caught up in the now. Part of that was necessity, part because it was different than everyone else, even ones like Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you did that section? Like I said, I really enjoyed it. I just don't like that it feels like Hunters know more about Sin-eaters than they know about themselves. And, yeah, the problem seems to be that Sin-eaters... only got one book. Like one and a half, if you count <i>Book of the Dead</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=134619#post134619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps you didn't understand my meaning:<br /> <br /> <i><b>That isn't how the game concept actually works and by giving credence to the notion that it does you are either deliberately lying or at the very least thoughtlessly propagating misinformation.</b></i><br /> <br /> That's not a matter of feelings so much as basic epistemic ethics.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not understanding something right, then perhaps you can enlighten me. Because as I understand it, the way krewe channels work only feels right for the Sacrosanct--the group of antagonists who explicitly believe their geister are angels and gods and that everyone else who's geister tell them they're angels or gods should die--and not for the player characters who are presumably of a more reasonable bent. As is, though, I agree with the Lucifuge:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lucifuge</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the haunted are rare, the Lucifuge have encountered enough of them over the years to study and form an opinion of them. The conspiracy reached the general conclusion that the ghostwalkers are, in fact, delusional. After all, the haunted\u2019s claims about how they managed to acquire an angelic or demonic patron were full of shit. Sure, ghostwalkers may <i>think</i> they\u2019ve made a contract with a divine being. The Lucifuge has had plenty of time, however, to figure out that there\u2019s a lot the haunted don\u2019t know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a fan of playing obviously deluded characters. While Mages have symbols to invoke and call upon, and werewolf packs have totemic spirits, they aren't told by the book that the revelations they receive are often believed as being given to them by gods, saints, demons, or Loa. Heck, rereading the first bit on the krewe channel again just now, it feels like it could have really benefited from being more like the way that werewolf packs work, especially in regards to bans, which is hinted at but not really elaborated on in Geist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foolish Milex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=134620#post134620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if only there was a way fans of Geist could pool our money in advance for further Geist books, to guarantee that they won't be made at a loss...</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be so happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T19:18:56-07:00","id":134816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=134728#post134728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm not understanding something right, then perhaps you can enlighten me. Because as I understand it, the way krewe channels work only feels right for the Sacrosanct--the group of antagonists who explicitly believe their geister are angels and gods and that everyone else who's geister tell them they're angels or gods should die--and not for the player characters who are presumably of a more reasonable bent.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sacrosanct are defined by <i>being dangerous fanatics</i>, not by believing their krewe channels to be the One True Way. It's right there in the lexicon and it's the entire reason they're notable as a classification of antagonist.<br /> <br /> None of this has anything to do with how &quot;your geist completely changes&quot; is an uncharitable and unsupported reading of the way gaining an Aspect works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As is, though, I agree with the Lucifuge:<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of playing obviously deluded characters. </div> </div> </div>Please never interact with religious people if your definition of &quot;obviously deluded&quot; is &quot;a member of the supernatural umbrella grouping that has one of the smallest views of the setting's cosmology found the claims of a supernatural group (which has illusions and occultation as a fifth of its primary power-lenses) about the nature of their mythology wanting and concluded that they possess holes in their knowledge (which is true of basically everybody considering that mystery is a major theme of the nWoD as a whole).&quot;<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters don't have a definite clue what empowers their channels. Their mythologies give them a symbolset that works for their individual understanding of the Underworld and the dead. The Lucifuge aren't ghostwalkers or any other type of mainline supernatural or reasonable facsimile thereof. &quot;These guys believe things that as near as we can tell are folkloric garbage&quot; is about as far as the average Hunter game needs to take that aspect of the group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While Mages have symbols to invoke and call upon, and werewolf packs have totemic spirits, they aren't told by the book that the revelations they receive are often believed as being given to them by gods, saints, demons, or Loa. </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are initiated into a society where the nearest thing to a definite line of descent that can be drawn as concerns their creation myth is the Firstborn, who are called out as pushing their own agendas just as often. A distressing number of the powerful Forsaken the line presents are called out as dangerously insane. The Supernal literally can't be experienced as it actually is because to do so would at best obliterate you without a perceptual filter. There's Verges from the Shadow that enforce particular types of forms on spirits that leave through them, and abilities exist that allow spirits to assume forms that adhere to the mythological and religious beliefs of the people who observe them. The Astral explicitly contains multiple versions of archetypal figures that vary by audience. The Phantasmal Key trucks with revelatory and obfuscatory illusions, the Stillness Key lets the dead control what people overlook, the Passion Key plays merry havoc with the significance people afford to things, and all of these are a sampler of what the power of the Underworld can allow one to do.<br /> <br /> And your problem is with people who went through the traumatic experience of dying and coming back to life with a mysterious and alien being getting a guidepost from the place said alien being trucks with to explain what the everloving Erebus is going on because it explicitly might not be true.<br /> <br /> Pardon my eyebrow as it scrapes the fucking ceiling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heck, rereading the first bit on the krewe channel again just now, it feels like it could have really benefited from being more like the way that werewolf packs work, especially in regards to bans, which is hinted at but not really elaborated on in Geist. </div> </div> </div>Your meaning is unclear here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-12-2014, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T19:44:50-07:00","id":134829,"title":"","content":"Wow that turned hostile fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T01:14:57-07:00","id":135100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=134728#post134728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, you did that section? Like I said, I really enjoyed it. I just don't like that it feels like Hunters know more about Sin-eaters than they know about themselves. And, yeah, the problem seems to be that Sin-eaters... only got one book. Like one and a half, if you count <i>Book of the Dead</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote that section, yes.<br /> <br /> The Loyalists know a lot about Sin-Eaters as they are scholars and Sin-Eaters were running rampant at their time of genesis, or close to it. There are undoubtedly scholarly Krewes who know more than they do. The thing is the Sin-Eaters, unlike say Vampires, have not had a single society going back through the ages, so some groups really know more than others. And to be fair, most Hunters don't know that Sin-Eaters exist at all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T01:36:19-07:00","id":135109,"title":"","content":"Satchel, please stop nit-picking at the dude. He's just trying to contribute to the community and the gameline. Personally, I found the concern about Sin-Eaters unwaveringly believing in their mythos, to be kinda corny too. Not for the same reason as Aspel, but i found it alittle corny all the same. As he said, he isn't hoping to rewrite Geist, but rather to propose alternatives and add-on's to what is pressented in the main book. If you disagree with his points of contention, then that's fine. We get that. Now please stop spewing poisonous fumes in here.You're getting the thread all nasty.<br /> <br /> Now, on to the actual thing. I always figured that Plasm's innitial conception, as hard to get so that Sin-Eaters would be incentavised to interact with Ghosts and enter the Underworld? Obviously, since Haunts was fixed to provide Plasm more frequently, i can see that this wasn't the case, which I didn't nessesarily have a problem with, but it surprised me.<br /> I've always emphasized heavily in my games, that Sin-Eaters are guardians of the balance between life and death. They dont help ghosts because they feel sorry for them (some might), but rather because they view them as existing in a wierd quasi-death-quasi-living state, that is detrimental to some great cosmic Underworld jamboree. Sorta like Wereworlf. I think this thread of logic is mentioned, though not emphasized very heavily in the book itself.<br /> To this end, Abmortals, and Immortals, pressent a very annoying quantity to Sin-Eaters. They're people who've sat all over the order they're trying to protect. Thats a point of conflict in and of itself, when their Geist tells them that this Immortal dude is an asshole, and deserves to shown to a Kerberoi.<br /> I've always figured Cthonians were just a wierd catch-all term for dead things that was mysterious as fuck. So a Mage might concievably view a Kerberoi as a Cthonian, since he probably dosen't what the hell it is. It is dead though. So its a Cthonian!<br /> I agree though. Even if we concede that the Kerberoi are Cthonian, we still need some more of them, which aren't Kerberoi.<br /> <br /> What I'de like to more off, is conflict with the Geist. The book Inferno had a cool minor-ish template called The Posessed, which were dudes claimed by demons from Hell (Not the God-Machine Demons. Actual Sinful Cruel and Evil demons from the actual Hell.), which I've been trying to implement in my own Geist games.<br /> <br /> I'll keep a close eye on this thread, and throw a few things sugestions in here when I think of them. Best of luck dude. I greatly appreciate your inniciative.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T03:19:06-07:00","id":135173,"title":"","content":"If you start a thread by calling a fairly important part of the setting a problem then you really shouldn't be all that surprised when people disagree with you and the thread gets side-tracked; it happens all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T06:10:04-07:00","id":135289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=135173#post135173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you start a thread by calling a fairly important part of the setting a problem then you really shouldn't be all that surprised when people disagree with you and the thread gets side-tracked; it happens all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh.It is overly hostile though, isn't it?<br /> <br /> The problem is they're both right: just about different things. By the letter of the law, there's nothing wrong with Krewe channels. It's the example given in the book that leads to people getting upset and throwing fits over the system. In practice though, the Krewe system is open ended: your Krewe's pseudo religion is only what the players make it. Don't want to make your Geist santa clause? Don't. You can just as easily come up with a basic, an inoffensive pseudo religion based on a mix of athiest concepts and Buddhism. If your keys are your connection to death and synergy is how in sync you are with your Geist, the channel is really just the synergy between each of the founders Geists. <br /> <br /> The real problem is that in today's society, religion is a touchy subject. Giving players any sort of freedom in this regard is probably not a good idea. The community could probably really benefit from a few more examples or even alternative rules for Krewe channels being put out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T09:36:17-07:00","id":135428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foolish Milex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=134620#post134620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if only there was a way fans of Geist could pool our money in advance for further Geist books, to guarantee that they won't be made at a loss...</div> </div> </div> </div>... ahem...<br /> <br /> Seriously, couldn't Onyx/CCP/WW use kickstarter to actually guage interest, rather than using it for the collectors editions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T11:03:22-07:00","id":135531,"title":"","content":"Santa Geist was just an example a friend of a friend gave to highlight how odd it is within the setting that your Sin-eater is meant to believe the geist, no matter how ridiculous their &quot;revealed form&quot; is. I think the problem is how it's written feels like your character is going to believe whatever the Channel is as being true, even if they don't agree with the actual channel ethos or anything. I like the religious aspect of it, I just don't like the whole transformative process. I prefer the idea of a krewe channel to be one that's actually LESS of a mechanical thing. It's been a while since I read Mage stuff, but for instance, I don't remember the cabal process being anything more than varying levels of formality between hanging out together and having gang signs to a long legal treatise. It feels like krewes would benefit more from that, as opposed to this ceremony that &quot;reveals&quot; a truth about the world and changes their Geists, because that feels very... silly.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt feels like only the Sacrosanct, who are so fanatical, would believe wholeheartedly that their geist was revealing a &quot;true&quot; form, and imparting a real &quot;truth&quot;. Which is why I dislike the krewe channel as it's presented. If the way I look at it is that no one would believe it, then obviously I'm going to dislike that it's there, because I feel like a &quot;truth&quot; your characters don't believe is silly... but I also feel like they shouldn't believe it.<br /> <br /> As for what I mean by saying that krewes could be more like packs, the section introducing krewes and the channel talks about how they have banes and rules... but then goes to say that they don't actually <i>mean</i> anything and sin-eaters can choose to just ignore them. For Werewolves when they bond to a Totem as a pack, they get bonuses and have a bane that they have to stick to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=135100#post135100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is the Sin-Eaters, unlike say Vampires, have not had a single society going back through the ages, so some groups really know more than others. And to be fair, most Hunters don't know that Sin-Eaters exist at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason this bothers me so much is that the Twilight Network is such a prevalent thing. Sin-eaters don't have Covenants, they have something better: Twitter. So that they've had this thing that's a big aspect of their setting and is all about knowledge, but they don't really have anything about their history, that just feels hollow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T11:46:59-07:00","id":135605,"title":"","content":"The TN as more than warnings and sort of heads up notes or territory is fairly new, though. Sin-Eaters are poised for a renaissance, or failing that a waxing of power and influence as the internet takes off though.<br /> <br /> As for the channel, well, your Geist can restore you from the dead and give you potent powers, so people are going to be inclined to believe what it says. The santa argument is just going to turn people off from listening to what you have to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-13-2014, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T12:29:04-07:00","id":135657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ugh.It is overly hostile though, isn't it? </div> </div> </div>I kinda agreed with you before Aspel's last post...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Santa Geist was just an example a friend of a friend gave to highlight how odd it is within the setting that your Sin-eater is meant to believe the geist, no matter how ridiculous their &quot;revealed form&quot; is. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It feels like krewes would benefit more from that, as opposed to this ceremony that &quot;reveals&quot; a truth about the world and changes their Geists, because that feels very... silly. </div> </div> </div>Now I think Satchel called it exactly right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T13:58:55-07:00","id":135734,"title":"","content":"I'm not trying to convince people to feel the same way I do, I'm just trying to explain why I don't like it, and what some of the other complaints I've heard about it are. Like I said, I'm not forcing anyone to use my ideas.<br /> <br /> Whether it's Santa or Gabriel the Archangel or even Baron Samedi, when you see OTHER people walking around with those same Geists, and each one's got a <i>different</i> channel, it's very dogmatic to say &quot;those guys aren't right, we're right&quot;. <i>That</i> is why I feel that the sort of &quot;your geist takes on a mythic form&quot; part of the krewe channel, the part that's imparted to you simply from binding the krewe, that part just feels like something that makes Sacrosanct. It rubs me the wrong way, and so far I've ignored it in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T15:00:15-07:00","id":135766,"title":"","content":"I think I see the problem. You've failed to roleplay this out and you're using extremely non-realistic extreme examples.<br /> <br /> First of all, the revelation of the channel is not a Geist only thing from how I read it. It's a combination of a discovery of how the universe works combined with how the Geist/Sin-eater interpret it. If the end result is that the Geist is Santa Clause, their beliefs before the fact damn well better reflect that it was a possibility in some way. If I was the storyteller of a game where the Krewe decided that one of the Geists was Santa or something ridiculous I'd demand they roleplay it out and give me a damn good explanation. What's happening is the characters are getting new information regarding how the universe works and revising their religious views, not being brainwashed into thinking up is down. They would never come up with something one of them thought was ridiculous because it's their own interpretation of it.<br /> <br /> By the way, I should mention that even if your characters are athiest, they still have a religious view. It's the idea that even if you refuse to choose, you've still made a choice.<br /> <br /> Second is the idea that it's an immediate transformation because that's how the rules play it out. It's just like leveling: yeah, on paper it happens immediately, but realistically the Krewe is having the revelation and probably spending some time testing the limits and revising their opinions.<br /> <br /> So, as I said before, we could all benefit from a better example. Allow me to provide one.<br /> <hr /><br /> Tom is in a Group and they decide it's time to officially make it a Krewe: they've learned the ritual and have three Sin eaters who wish to be joined. Tom is an Athiest, Cindy is christian and Zach is a Buddhist.<br /> <br /> Out of character, they decide to come up with three channels that they can agree on: Suffering, celebration and balance.<br /> <br /> Tom chooses celebration since he believes religion is a lie used to manipulate people, and they should drop it and simply enjoy life. He believes thanks to his time as a sin-eater that there are beings that are truly more powerful out there (perhaps even god-like) but, like him, they simply exist and he owes them nothing and should spend his life living it for himself. His Geists channel is not the embodiment of Athiesm however: it's the embodiment of independence, free will and occasionally rebellion.<br /> <br /> Cindy chooses suffering: she believes there IS a higher power and that we should live our lives for him or her. Her Geist is also not the embodiment of Christianity: it's the embodiment of hard work, dedication and fighting for a greater cause, in slight opposition to Tom's. <br /> <br /> Finally, Zach will represent balance: believing that there's a time and place for both suffering and celebration. His Geist represents balance, peace and tranquility.<br /> <br /> Now, out of character the players have come to an agreement: their in character religions are not the same to be overly specific, so instead they decide to come up with something sensible: the Geists discover they are aspects of the Judges: the ones that wrote the old laws of the underworld and are divinely mandated to judge the living and dead. Their creation myth is that the universe came into being when a great surge of power caused creation. Other options would be that the universe always existed and is simply self perpetuating. Or maybe they get more abstract and say the universe was once a very simple spirit: the only thing that existed. It became sentiant and the paradox of its existance caused it to splinter into three main ideas: Suffering, Celebration and Balance. These three entities set about building the universe as we know it out of themselves in order to discover the solution to the original paradox of its existance. Knowing what they know about the universe, the players agree that whatever they chose fits in with their characters belief systems.<br /> <br /> The end result: the Geists are more or less who they were before, but with a slight tilt to their sense of existence. It also gives the storyteller new themes to work with: perhaps their in an unbalance in the world and the SEs have to investigate why a town is suddenly too much balance in South Dekota, or not enough suffering in the underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T20:45:40-07:00","id":136159,"title":"","content":"I'm aware of how it works. I just don't <i>like</i> how it works. There also isn't a channel for each Sin-eater, but one for the entire krewe as a whole. The reason I don't like the krewe channel is because no matter what the krewe channel is, it's &quot;wrong&quot;. It isn't a deep and powerful Truth of the world. It's a lie. Whether it's intentionally a lie by the Geists or not, it's still just bunk. It feels hollow to me and silly that every krewe is going to have it's own truth about the creation myth and it's geists take on new aspects. Whether it happens instantly or over a day doesn't matter--although the example in the book certainly seems to imply it happens instantly--because the Geists reveal that they were always some other person in hiding. And Sin-eaters one and all seem to if not believe it entirely still seem to buy into the importance of the Channel.<br /> <br /> When I say &quot;the Geist was secretly Santa all along&quot;, I'm using an intentionally exaggerated example. Whether your Geist says that it's Santa Claus or Marqui de Sade, though, the fact that the channel is something that is verifiably false within the setting--I once again point out the Lucifuge saying the Ghostwalkers are deluded--bothers me. It isn't something like the Atlantis myth or the origin of the Lineages. The first time any reasonable, rational minded Sin-eater goes to a Flesh Fair and talks to another krewe they should realize &quot;these people all have channels that were revealed to them by their geists, just like my krewe was&quot;, and that if <i>those </i>people are being lied to, it stands to reason that <i>this</i> krewe is being lied to as well.<br /> <br /> That's why I don't like it. Because the game tells you &quot;this was revealed by your psyche so you believe it&quot;. That's something that doesn't sit well with me. I don't care if the channel reveals the <i>actual</i> history of the world, that it comes in this flash of insight that takes months or years to fully understand, but you <i>believe</i> it, even if you don't agree with it, that bothers me. Yes, it says that some sin-eaters reject the Channel, and some don't believe their Geists are actually Santa Claus or Marqui de Sade (de Sade actually is the example they give, which I actually find sillier than Santa Claus. At least Father Winter has something to do with Death), but the fact that the Geist says that in the first place, and the fact that it changes to show that, taking on that Aspect, is to me as ridiculous as Predator's Taint. I am honestly legitimately surprised that &quot;I don't like the way krewe channels work&quot; is getting so much heat. I have never met anyone who actually liked them, and when I've seen them used in play, the channel is treated more as something like a cabal's beliefs: From the characters, and easily reconciled with other people's beliefs. A cabal uses the elements as symbols, and their elemental powers are stronger simply because symbols have power.<br /> <br /> I <i>like</i> the idea of Bound krewes being half gang, half cult. But I <i>don't</i> like the idea that my character is encouraged to have a giant blind spot.<br /> <br /> As they're written, the only people who seem like they'd believe their channel are the Sacrosanct. The channel itself feels less like a great revelation about the world and more like baggage that characters don't need. It feels tacked on, and pointless, and I have legitimately never seen other players defend it. I don't feel that it's the source of the game's mythology. The Underworld is. Ghosts are. The krewe channel, <i>in my opinion</i>, and from what I have seen from other players, adds nothing of value to the game. At best it adds a source of conflict--and indeed the book says that conflict is the whole point of the channel--but that source of conflict and narrative drama comes at the cost of forcing the characters to be willfully ignorant. And that rubs me, and the majority of other players I've talked to, the wrong way. It's something decided OOC, but it's forced on your characters IC.<br /> <br /> More than that, it completely rewrites the geist. Almost every Sin-eater concept I've had has been strongly tied to what their geist <i>is right now</i>. The Old Man of the Mountain hashshashin who molds his sin-eater into an Assassin, publicly murdering mafia bosses to strike fear into their hearts. The Wicked Witch who watches over the young Bound and helps her grow into a <i>bruja </i>who speaks for the dead. La Llarona the Weeping Whore with her bloody wrists and wet nightgown who encourages her Reaper to kill bad husbands and rapists and abusive boyfriends. The beautiful Dionysian man with wine stained lips and denarian eyes who wants to fight and fuck and double down on gambling and get drunk off his ass with the help of his Bound. None of those were even part of krewes, much less involved in a channel. I don't see the point of waiting until my character becomes part of a krewe to have the geist I <i>really</i> wanted.<br /> <br /> I really don't know how I can be more clear about it. This is an aspect of the setting that I don't like. It isn't that I don't understand it, it's that I do and don't like the implications of it within the setting. I have met several other players that have complained about it as well, which is one of the reasons I put it on my list of things to 'fix'. I am frankly getting a little irritated about this, because I keep having to explain why I don't like something over and over. There is no aspect of the krewe channel that I like. I find the Creation Myth to be a silly and unnecessary part. I find the Metaphysics equally unnecessary as something so important. I find the Aspects that Geists take on to be <i>completely</i> unnecessary and I have never seen a krewe use that, even if they were using any of the other parts of the channel rules. I suppose I have no problem with the Symbols. The Ethos, that has potential to be interesting, but there are no real mechanics to it and the book even mentions that the Ethos is as meaningless to some krewe members as &quot;don't take cookies from the cookie jar&quot; because the Ethos can and is ignored. I also feel like the Krewe merits add nothing and could for the most part be regular merits. <br /> <br /> I don't like the krewe rules. I understand them completely, I just don't like them. Nothing anyone says is likely to change my mind. I honestly didn't think I'd have to defend that opinion, and I certainly didn't think that would become the biggest point of contention in the thread. I'm sorry if this comes off as hostile, but it kind of feels like I'm being dogpiled here.<br /> <br /> I just want to address most of the complaints I've heard about Geist from other players, and from people who don't like it because of those problems (&quot;there's no focus or antagonists or <i>point</i>&quot; being the biggest, because dealing with ghosts is not as interesting as, say, the Seers or Banishers or the Pure or Pandorans or Hobgoblins or Idigam).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:37:39-07:00","id":136286,"title":"","content":"I'll make this as quick and blunt as I can:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=136159#post136159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>The massive outpouring of skepticism to the contrary and your stated understanding of how it works being at odds with how the book actually presents it \u2014 and likewise your presenting things the book actually describes as the case as changes you would make \u2014 should speak for itself, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There also isn't a channel for each Sin-eater, but one for the entire krewe as a whole. </div> </div> </div>And it's synthesized out of the beliefs of no more than ten people plus whatever weird contributions those people's geister contribute to make the channel tilt the game toward the type of stories the players want to tell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason I don't like the krewe channel is because no matter what the krewe channel is, it's &quot;wrong&quot;. It isn't a deep and powerful Truth of the world. It's a lie. Whether it's intentionally a lie by the Geists or not, it's still just bunk. </div> </div> </div>It's &quot;bunk&quot; <i>that still gives them power and connections.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It feels hollow to me and silly that every krewe is going to have it's own truth about the creation myth and it's geists take on new aspects. Whether it happens instantly or over a day doesn't matter--although the example in the book certainly seems to imply it happens instantly--because the Geists reveal that they were always some other person in hiding. And Sin-eaters one and all seem to if not believe it entirely still seem to buy into the importance of the Channel. </div> </div> </div>The channel <i>is</i> important. &quot;True&quot; or not, it gives its founders a symbolset that taps into a power source that their krewe's mythology provides the most resonant explanation for.<br /> <br /> When the Mad Hatter reveals himself to be the prophetic aspect of the god Odin reaching across time and distance to try once more to avert the apocalypse, that doesn't change anything about him other than the significance afforded to some of the things he says. When Rubberneck lets slip that he is a representative of the primal car crash's first innocent bystander, he doesn't stop being the headless traffic cop that Phillip made a Bargain with after his tumble over the asphalt. It doesn't much matter whether or not Gary Gearbox actually believes that ghosts are the Void's dreams of the World and the Underworld is the World's dream of the Void, but it's the explanation that makes the most intuitive sense to him because that cosmology is drawn from his head and the heads of the rest of the Insomniacs and their geists.<br /> <br /> Geister are occulted figures who often have massive gaps in their memory. Gaining an Aspect is as simple as filling in some of those gaps. That's why apocalyptic epiphany is the primary mechanism through which the characters Bound to them acquire their channels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I say &quot;the Geist was secretly Santa all along&quot;, I'm using an intentionally exaggerated example. </div> </div> </div><b>And this was a dumb, shitty, counterproductive thing to do.</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether your Geist says that it's Santa Claus or Marqui de Sade, though, the fact that the channel is something that is verifiably false within the setting--I once again point out the Lucifuge saying the Ghostwalkers are deluded--bothers me. </div> </div> </div>Okay, here's the thing: pay close attention to the Lucifuge's point of &quot;verifiable falsity&quot; \u2014 they're pretty much saying &quot;these people claim to have received a revelation from an angel or a demon, but it's no sort of angel or demon that we've heard of, and we've heard of quite a few.&quot;<br /> <br /> And <i>again</i>: Hunters are not experts on the supernatural as a whole, and Sin-Eaters in particular are a strange and ill-understood facet of the supernatural. Their assessments of the beliefs of the supernatural genus associated with the realm that is arguably the nWoD's most mysterious zone within relatively easy reach should be taken with at least as many grains of salt as any other &quot;objective&quot; assessment of the true nature of a splat's metaphysics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It isn't something like the Atlantis myth or the origin of the Lineages. </div> </div> </div><i>It is <b>precisely that.</b> </i>The seed of it, at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first time any reasonable, rational minded Sin-eater goes to a Flesh Fair and talks to another krewe they should realize &quot;these people all have channels that were revealed to them by their geists, just like my krewe was&quot;, and that if <i>those </i>people are being lied to, it stands to reason that <i>this</i> krewe is being lied to as well. </div> </div> </div>The mention that several <i>geists</i> in the modern era are &quot;up-front&quot; about the krewe channel being a psychodrama to bind the krewe into a cohesive unit in combination with Bound culture's general tendency to use elements of culture because it suits them would seem to indicate you're assuming a much more rigid faith than exists in the typical Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, it says that some sin-eaters reject the Channel, and some don't believe their Geists are actually Santa Claus or Marqui de Sade (de Sade actually is the example they give, which I actually find sillier than Santa Claus. At least Father Winter has something to do with Death), but the fact that the Geist says that in the first place, and the fact that it changes to show that, taking on that Aspect, is to me as ridiculous as Predator's Taint. </div> </div> </div>That you find the notion of a geist claiming to be the ghost of <i>the guy whose beliefs included extreme freedom unbound by religion, law, or morality and whose contributions to the cultural zeitgeist include making his name into an adjective for people who enjoy violence</i> has nothing to do with death speaks volumes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am honestly legitimately surprised that &quot;I don't like the way krewe channels work&quot; is getting so much heat. I have never met anyone who actually liked them, and when I've seen them used in play, the channel is treated more as something like a cabal's beliefs: From the characters, and easily reconciled with other people's beliefs. A cabal uses the elements as symbols, and their elemental powers are stronger simply because symbols have power. </div> </div> </div><i>That is exactly how a krewe channel works.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More than that, it completely rewrites the geist. Almost every Sin-eater concept I've had has been strongly tied to what their geist <i>is right now</i>. The Old Man of the Mountain hashshashin who molds his sin-eater into an Assassin, publicly murdering mafia bosses to strike fear into their hearts. The Wicked Witch who watches over the young Bound and helps her grow into a <i>bruja </i>who speaks for the dead. La Llarona the Weeping Whore with her bloody wrists and wet nightgown who encourages her Reaper to kill bad husbands and rapists and abusive boyfriends. The beautiful Dionysian man with wine stained lips and denarian eyes who wants to fight and fuck and double down on gambling and get drunk off his ass with the help of his Bound. None of those were even part of krewes, much less involved in a channel. I don't see the point of waiting until my character becomes part of a krewe to have the geist I <i>really</i> wanted. </div> </div> </div>I've written on this viewpoint elsewhere. Suffice it to be said that <a href=\"http://wonsab.tumblr.com/post/31829000006/wrote-this-elsewhere-figured-i-may-as-well-paste-it\" target=\"_blank\">I don't have much respect for it.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really don't know how I can be more clear about it. This is an aspect of the setting that I don't like. It isn't that I don't understand it, it's that I do and don't like the implications of it within the setting. I have met several other players that have complained about it as well, which is one of the reasons I put it on my list of things to 'fix'. I am frankly getting a little irritated about this, because I keep having to explain why I don't like something over and over. There is no aspect of the krewe channel that I like. I find the Creation Myth to be a silly and unnecessary part. I find the Metaphysics equally unnecessary as something so important. I find the Aspects that Geists take on to be <i>completely</i> unnecessary and I have never seen a krewe use that, even if they were using any of the other parts of the channel rules. I suppose I have no problem with the Symbols. The Ethos, that has potential to be interesting, but there are no real mechanics to it and the book even mentions that the Ethos is as meaningless to some krewe members as &quot;don't take cookies from the cookie jar&quot; because the Ethos can and is ignored. I also feel like the Krewe merits add nothing and could for the most part be regular merits.<br /> <br /> I don't like the krewe rules. I understand them completely, I just don't like them. Nothing anyone says is likely to change my mind. I honestly didn't think I'd have to defend that opinion, and I certainly didn't think that would become the biggest point of contention in the thread. I'm sorry if this comes off as hostile, but it kind of feels like I'm being dogpiled here. </div> </div> </div>You frame your misinformed opinions as a general fix using a deliberately terrible argument and make the first mistake of opinion-having by trying to &quot;defend&quot; it (protip: if you are in fact as steadfast in holding this opinion as you claim to be then there is no need to defend it - any &quot;defense&quot; is instead an attempt to convince other people to share your opinion, despite your claims otherwise) and you're surprised when people find every further elaboration of your lack-of-understanding to be another reason to demonstrate that you don't know what you're talking about.<br /> <br /> I don't know what you expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T23:38:05-07:00","id":136363,"title":"","content":"Here is a thing:<br /> <br /> -Lucifuge are not experts on Geister. Geister are not Demons as the Lucifuge understands them. But then, so aren't some other things we would call Demons.<br /> <br /> -Many Sin-Eater powers, according to those with knowlage of magic and metaphysics, should not work. No way the Giggling Scarecrow should be an aspect of Hecate. But when she says she is, she has the power to back it up. When the Sin-Eaters do Ceremonies that fly in the face of what Occultists say should work and they do, it means something is going on...it likely does not mean the Sin-Eaters are the ones confused about reality.<br /> <br /> The answer likley lies in the Great Below. Are Sin-Eaters actually tapping into something down there? Maybe they are. Something is happening, and those who say &quot;they are foolish to believe that these beings could be the mythic beings they say they are&quot; are ignoring the fact that the channels work, that Ceremonies work, that everything about Sin-Eaters suggests that those dismissing them don't understand something fundamental about them. Maybe Odin is part of a dead world that is communicating from the Lower Depths through the Geist. Maybe his power is being channeled by Sin-Eaters through their strange ceremonies.<br /> <br /> We don't, and probably won't, know for sure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T06:38:11-07:00","id":136621,"title":"","content":"I think I'm with Satchel on this, and I like how Baron put it, but I feel it needs more explanation. <i>As an aside: Aspel, I think you're allowing your personal views of religion seep into your opinion. If you are unable to handle the religious aspects of Geist, I recommend you don't try: <b>but don't phrase it as 'fixing the system for everyone' if you do.</b> It tends to annoy people who know the system a hell of a lot better than you do. </i>Anyways, to the heart of the matter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=136159#post136159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether your Geist says that it's Santa Claus or Marqui de Sade, though, the fact that the channel is something that is verifiably false within the setting--I once again point out the Lucifuge saying the Ghostwalkers are deluded--bothers me. It isn't something like the Atlantis myth or the origin of the Lineages</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's where you get it wrong: it's not verifiably false. It's just an interpretation of reality from someone who, although they might be a little unhinged, has seen a lot more of the picture of reality then you have. Think of it like this: Understanding reality is a giant puzzle, and you don't even have a fifth of the pieces. Humanity comes up with science principles and understandings to piece together the pieces it does have and assumes the finished product is all there is... then someone becomes a sin eater and finds a few more pieces (the underworld and ghosts) - they suddenly believe something that is - according to you - verifiably false. But slowly, they accept this and come up with ways to justify connecting it to the puzzle pieces humanity is pretty sure we've put together. <br /> <br /> Then one day, the Geist comes out and reveals some more of the puzzle pieces that the sin-eater needs to know - just a bit, and distorted by our narrow human perspective. Hell, they might not even be connected to any of the pieces you've put together so far as part of your understanding of the universe. To make things worse, you can only interpret it based on your personal perspective of the universe: so the Geist puts it into terms the Sin-eater can understand: 'I am an aspect of Michael the Angel, here to guard the gates'. Or 'I am the Marqui de Sade - here to push boundaries and teach people to celebrate life'.<br /> <br /> And of course different people react differently: some take it literally and assume that their Geist is the one and only Santa Clause. Others might be willing to interpret it in a more abstract sense (he is an aspect of a force of the universe that is personified in human lore as an Angel of God sent to guard the gates of heaven - whatever that actually means is still beyond my understanding.) Some will accept that they really can only see some small part of the big picture, while others will say 'OK, yup. I now know everything. Anyone who says anything that doesn't fit into the picture that I have is lying and deserves death, or at least a lot of ridicule'<br /> <br /> Why do the Geists do this? Perhaps they're releasing a little bit of the truth to show their relationship to each of the other Krewe members in order to cement the bond. Perhaps it's to help the Sin-Eater to understand why Geists act the way they do, or are who they are. Perhaps they do have the full picture themselves of the universe, or perhaps they too have only seen part of the puzzle, but its a different part of the puzzle than you've seen, so they're showing you more. Or maybe they're batshit crazy and the ceramony is just showing you a part of the alien entity because why not?<br /> <br /> Again though, this is really a lot like actual religion and requires a lot of open-mindedness that many people are not able to do. Some people <i>like</i> abstract concepts though, it gives them a broader setting to write stories in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T11:46:15-07:00","id":136930,"title":"","content":"Satchel, I said several times that I'm not forcing anyone to play this. It's &quot;fixing the system for everyone&quot; who feels the same way I do. More than that, no, Santa Claus as an example is not a &quot;dumb, shitty, counterproductive thing to do&quot;, because Santa Claus has more to do with death than the Marqui de Sade, namesakes aside. Furthermore, no, the geists do actually change to take on these new aspects, as is shown by the examples in the book. Your tumblr link also amounts to saying nothing. In fact, &quot;geists can change because they're <i>ghost stories</i>&quot; is as canon as my way of ignoring the krewe channel altogether. Should I keep going? Because no, the krewe channel is nothing like cabal symbolism, because that doesn't come down from on high, the cabal itself, in character, creates it. The krewe channel on the other hand is from the geist, the krewe's psyche, etcetera, and they have no in-character say in it. Also, you're frankly ignoring the actual problem I have with it: There are going to be sin-eaters who both have Marqui de Sade or Santa Claus or the Archangel Michael. <i>Their</i> version of Marqui de Sade or Santa Claus or the Archangel Michael is going to be different than <i>my</i> version of Marqui de Sade or Santa Claus or the Archangel Michael, and tell them something different. They'll have the same Aspect but a completely different krewe channel.<br /> <br /> Now, if I'm a person in the world, obviously seeing someone who <i>also</i> has Marqui de Sade or Santa Claus or the Archangel Michael as their geist is going to make me think &quot;woah, this isn't right!&quot;<br /> If I'm a rational human being, I will realize that maybe none of it is real and that despite the fact that I feel I learned some fundamental truth of the universe, it was all make believe. Which completely invalidates the krewe channel as it exists.<br /> If I'm <i>not</i> a rational human being, then I believe that despite the staggering odds against it, my krewe channel is correct, and my version of Marqui de Sade or Santa Claus or the Archangel Michael is the <i>real</i> one--or the head one, or the one acting as go between from me to the real one--and that those <i>other</i> versions of Marqui de Sade or Santa Claus or the Archangel Michael are lying and need to die before they cause trouble. And I become one of the <i>Sacrosanct</i>.<br /> <b><i>This is the problem that I have with it.</i></b> You either realize your krewe channel isn't absolute truth, which invalidates the whole thing (at that point it might as well be treated as an in-character thing, as opposed to an out of character thing) or you become Sacrosanct. Or at the very least you believe, despite the obvious, that you're right, even if you aren't dangerous about it.<br /> <br /> It isn't the Lucifuge that invalidates the krewe channel and makes it verifiably false, I just like that they point out that to anyone who's done actual research these might-as-well-be-Sacrosanct sin-eaters who wholly believe their Geists <i>are incompetent and ignoring any research</i>. No, what makes the krewe channel something you can verify as false, or at the very least questionable, <i><b>is the existence of other krewes with different channels</b></i>. <br /> <br /> And no, this has nothing to do with me being close minded to other religions. Because other religions aren't revealed to you, personally, by magic ghosts. You can also join or leave a religion that you agree with, and you don't have a &quot;no, that's impossible!&quot; Luke-I-Am-Your-Father reaction upon the 'reveal' of your krewe channel, the way that the example of a proper Christian who's krewe channel is Satanistic will. You also can't interact with the magical ghosts that say your version of Christianity is the best and that the <i>other</i> magical ghost, who says their version of Christianity is the best, is totally lying (and you should probably kill him).<br /> <br /> I again point to cabals. Their mythos is formed in character. There is no magical ghost assuring them that their way is the right way. They have no &quot;proof&quot;. They are, effectively, the same as mortal religions. And I like it much better. I would prefer if the krewe channel worked like that, instead of the book telling you that Marqui de Sade or Santa Claus or the Archangel Michael is revealing the nature of the world to you.<br /> <br /> Now I'd really rather we just didn't talk about this. Because, frankly, Satchel, you're overtly hostile and your argument amounts to &quot;your interpretation of the book is wrong, mine is right&quot;. Which, in addition to making me realize why Moochava avoids RPGnet is also somewhat relevant to this ridiculous discussion. The reason I'm defending my opinion is because you verbally attacked me in your first post and you've continued to do as much, calling me stupid, that I fail at ethics, and your entire rhetoric more or less amounting to treating me as if I'm literally lying because your version of things--which, everything you said in that Tumblr post is <b><i>your personal, non-canonical opinion</i></b>--and that naturally makes people want to defend themselves. So I ask you politely to drop the subject. You like the krewe channel. That's fine. No one is making you change it. I am <i>not</i> actually trying to make you share my opinion, simply to explain <i>why</i> I have that opinion. Again, it's an opinion I've commonly heard before. The topic at hand is &quot;what do you think should be changed about Geist as it is now&quot;. You are apparently ready to violently defend the krewe channel. Okay. But what <i>do</i> you think should be changed or expanded on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T12:12:08-07:00","id":136965,"title":"","content":"The amount of not-listening you're doing is approaching critical levels, so I'm going to leave a <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaulteae8-8.html?g=posts&amp;m=283305#post283305\" target=\"_blank\">couple links</a> from <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default9172-6.html?g=posts&amp;m=283309#post283309\" target=\"_blank\">the guy who wrote the section on krewes</a> and wait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T13:28:39-07:00","id":137092,"title":"","content":"Yes, that's all well and good, word from the author. Except that it changes nothing. You aren't listening yourself. It isn't that I don't understand. Nothing Malcolm said there is new to me. The issue at hand is that <i>I do not like it</i>. <br /> <br /> You can keep presenting things to me in a house or with a mouse or on a boat or with a goat, but the thing is I've already tried the green eggs and ham and didn't like them, Sam I Am.<br /> <br /> Put in simple and explicit terms: I do not like the krewe channel. I do not feel it adds anything worthwhile to the game. What it <i>could</i> add to the game can be done better without it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T13:36:26-07:00","id":140894,"title":"","content":"I don't think that really bears further arguing since it comes down to not liking it, and that's not something that can be argued away. Do you have any thoughts on how you want to change the Krewe channels and the like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T14:38:18-07:00","id":140942,"title":"","content":"Mostly changing the krewe channel to be more organic, and more in character. Less of a binary &quot;channel/no channel&quot; thing and more like cabals, how they're something the characters actively choose for themselves, as opposed to something that they have chosen for them by their psyches. The emphasis on the unconscious nature of the channel is what I don't like.<br /> <br /> Bound krewes would be ones who have this mystical &quot;blood brother&quot; pact going on, sort of like a Changeling's motley or a Uratha pack. I'd like to see the mechanics of a krewe be something similar to that. They also go on about the Ethos, but nothing actually binds a krewe to it, the way that a werewolf Totem's ban does. Giving the krewe that adheres to it's own ethos a bonus to plasm generation and one that goes against it a &quot;leakage&quot; of plasm seems like a good place to start on that front.<br /> <br /> My main problem with the channel is just that it comes from an out of character place, and feels kind of forced upon the characters. Even if you make a krewe channel the characters approve of, how it comes about rubs me the wrong way. All of it being in character (and with the Aspects being less what the geist are and more what they already represent, c.f.: Ill Sabbah, La Llarona, the Wicked Witch) feels more appropriate. The krewe binding ceremony, then, would be a mystical enforcement of the krewe's beliefs and ethos, empowering their symbols and ethos with psyche in exchange for giving them bonuses. Less a binding and more of an oath-taking, causing the plasm of the participants to mingle together. Less the geists saying &quot;here is the truth&quot; and more the krewe itself saying &quot;we agree this is the truth&quot;. The mingling of plasm amongst each other also enforces and highlights the cult and gang aspects.<br /> <br /> Plasm is thicker than blood or water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T15:58:31-07:00","id":140997,"title":"","content":"I've always looked at the Krewe channel, as a combination of &quot;The sheer force of belief combined with the magical nature of the Sin-Eaters psyche, magically forces arcane energies to realign and makes it true&quot; combined with &quot;It is true from the beginning&quot;. No matter the cause, in my interpritation, Krewes channels are never objectively wrong, because believing in something that is objectively wrong would be pants shittingly retarded.<br /> I personally think some of the charm of the Krewe channel, is that it has an 'out-of-character' touch to it. As i understand it, it is 50% made by the Geists (the 'out-of-character' part) and 50% by the characters, which would be an in-character part.<br /> The Geists dosen't so much reveal &quot;what they really are&quot; as they evolve into a new form that might better feed upon and draw strenght from the part of the channel the Sin-Eaters have created, and believe in. Akin to a spirit feeding upon something that it is a spirit of, the Geist becomes a spirit of the Krewe channel, and every action the Sin-Eaters undertake to strenghten the channel, strenghten the Geists. In this respect, it is actually the part the Sin-Eaters makes, which dictates the half that the Geists make, because the Geists merely evolve to better absorb power from the religious and philosophical beliefs of their Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> Like this, the Sacrosanct might seem like religious fanatics, but they're in actuality slaves/puppets/tools of power hungry Geists, who look to empower themselves by making their hosts practically insane with emotional fervor of the thing the Geist has become a quasi-spirit of.<br /> <br /> Thats my interpritation, anyway. Not trying to say this is the right way, or the best way. But its what I find is cool.<br /> Looking forward to seeing your interpritation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T17:34:55-07:00","id":141076,"title":"","content":"I don't really mind if a Geist was nuts enough to insist they exist for some sort of great hidden purpose, but I think that your Geist claiming he's Odin is kind of lame. If it's claiming to be something a bit more esoteric, that might be cooler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T19:18:46-07:00","id":141157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=141076#post141076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really mind if a Geist was nuts enough to insist they exist for some sort of great hidden purpose, but I think that your Geist claiming he's Odin is kind of lame.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://wonsab.tumblr.com/post/39795555121/drcthulwho-wonsab-drcthulwho-odin-and\" target=\"_blank\">wow excuse u</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it's claiming to be something a bit more esoteric, that might be cooler. </div> </div> </div>Odin's not esoteric?<br /> <br /> Odin, the guy the Interpretatio Germanica identifies with the Roman god of &quot;financial gain, commerce, eloquence (and thus poetry), messages/communication (including divination), travelers, boundaries, luck, trickery and thieves&quot;? The guy who made the world with his brothers from the corpse of the Primordial Man? The guy who sacrificed himself to himself to learn the magic of runes and gave his eye for wisdom and knowledge? The guy who spends much of his time preparing an army for a battle at the end of the world that he knows he will lose? <br /> <br /> Look, I realize the internet has made propagation of existing information a lot easier than it used to be, but I have to tilt my head at the notion that the Bound need to act like hipster-stereotypes and scoff at any secret history that has a recognizable name attached to it. A glimpse at the sample memorabilia alone should give you a hint of how much conspiratorial fakery the Bound can expect to see even without accounting for the massive game of whisper-down-the-lane that they work with. They're speakers for the dead, and the dead tend to warp a bit in the Underworld. Remember the Underworld? That place the krewe taps into to get their channels that realign the fate of their newborn organization?<br /> <br /> The point of the krewe channel is that it provides the starting grounds for an ongoing mystery around which the group's raison d'etre is built. That means the thing's meant to have layers of revelation over time. The names and associations of an Aspect are starting clues that will, by the nature of the channel's formation, have other clues scattered in the krewe's path in the form of significant ghosts, deaths, mementos, and so on.<br /> <br /> The Underworld's a giant entropic garbage heap and the Bound sift through and reorder it along with the land of the living through the guidance of their channels. That necessarily involves handling a decent quantity of bullshit before you get to something that passes for the whole truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T21:43:46-07:00","id":141242,"title":"","content":"Besides, I can think of nothing more in-character for certain Geists than to claim to be Odin. Satchel hit most of them on the head: mysterious/insane, deathy, sacrificial, not bound to traditional morality, full of weird magic and prophecies. Am I talking about Odin or geists?<br /> (both)<br /> (p.s. you don't want to see Loki the Gentry)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T23:20:27-07:00","id":141279,"title":"","content":"I'd say that Hel would be more appropriate for a Geist to claim to be, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=140997#post140997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like this, the Sacrosanct might seem like religious fanatics, but they're in actuality slaves/puppets/tools of power hungry Geists, who look to empower themselves by making their hosts practically insane with emotional fervor of the thing the Geist has become a quasi-spirit of.</div> </div> </div> </div>... My God. A Sacrosanct Wretched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T23:55:00-07:00","id":141288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=141157#post141157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://wonsab.tumblr.com/post/39795555121/drcthulwho-wonsab-drcthulwho-odin-and\" target=\"_blank\">wow excuse u</a><br /> <br /> Snip<br /> <br /> Look, I realize the internet has made propagation of existing information a lot easier than it used to be, but I have to tilt my head at the notion that the Bound need to act like hipster-stereotypes and scoff at any secret history that has a recognizable name attached to it.<br /> <br /> Snip</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough. I guess I'd be less bothered personally if they weren't claiming to be somebody that sounds like they have more important things to do than vicariously snort blow off ephemeral hooker butts as a Sin-Eater might do.<br /> <br /> If it's like his lesser known cousin Joe the Wise, servant of Odin and lesser God of Some Sort of Importance, I'm okay with that. But the real deal would seem to me to have bigger fish to fry, and wouldn't be a Geist.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I think &quot;an aspect of archangel gabriel&quot; is an easier sell, if nothing else because it implies the Geist is a component rather than the whole, and that strikes me as more sensible than simply suggesting it's Odin or Gabriel themselves. It's a little thing, but it helps.<br /> <br /> I'll also clarify that the concept doesn't bother me, some parts of it just don't really do it for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 05-18-2014, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T00:19:04-07:00","id":141296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=141288#post141288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's like his lesser known cousin Joe the Wise, servant of Odin and lesser God of Some Sort of Importance, I'm okay with that. But the real deal would seem to me to have bigger fish to fry, and wouldn't be a Geist.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I think &quot;an aspect of archangel gabriel&quot; is an easier sell, if nothing else because it implies the Geist is a component rather than the whole, and that strikes me as more sensible than simply suggesting it's Odin or Gabriel themselves. It's a little thing, but it helps.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aspects: Who are the mythology\u2019s personalities? The ceremony exalts the founders\u2019 geists, giving them mystic Aspects: elaborations of the archetypes they uphold. In many cases, the names and natures of the powers develop from the creation myth, but <b>the geists are not literal gods \u2014 or probably aren\u2019t, at least. Rather, the geist is an aspect of a god, archangel, or culture hero.</b> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, if the founder dies without marking a successor, his geist can select one by bonding to a new Sin-Eater, though this is rarely done. Some geists abandon the idea of bonding with a Sin-Eater after their experience with the founder, and it\u2019s said that some grow powerful enough to become deathlords. <b>They graduate from the avatars of death gods to gods themselves.</b> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Aspects are transferrable qualities.<br /> <br /> I mentioned the Interpretatio Germanica earlier but didn't elaborate - it's relevant: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;When they described the gods of Celtic and Germanic tribes, rather than considering them separate deities, the Romans interpreted them as <b>local manifestations or aspects of their own gods</b>, a cultural trait called the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interpretatio_Romana\" target=\"_blank\">interpretatio Romana</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interpretatio_graeca\" target=\"_blank\">.</a>&quot;<br /> <br /> Syncretism describes basically the entirety of Bound common-culture.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T10:08:17-07:00","id":141670,"title":"","content":"Thanks for explaining that, I'm feeling better about Krewe Channels with that understanding. I guess one last question that's worth asking: If your Geist were originally called something like the Raven Watcher or whatever, and your krewe channel had them saying they're really Odin, would that Aspect just be a component of their identity, or does it supplant their previous identity? Would he be Raven Watcher, Aspect of Odin, or would the Sin-Eater just call him Odin?<br /> <br /> Does a Sin-Eater know their Geists &quot;name&quot; anywho? I'm gonna go look in the book about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T15:30:15-07:00","id":141884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=141670#post141670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a Sin-Eater know their Geists &quot;name&quot; anywho? I'm gonna go look in the book about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The write ups all name the Geist, and the intro fluff, <i>Rum is the Drink the Dead Like Best</i>, has Cassie and Cason's geists named as the Red Seamstress and the Griefstruck Surgeon (both are good with needles).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T16:08:03-07:00","id":141892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=141670#post141670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for explaining that, I'm feeling better about Krewe Channels with that understanding. I guess one last question that's worth asking: If your Geist were originally called something like the Raven Watcher or whatever, and your krewe channel had them saying they're really Odin, would that Aspect just be a component of their identity, or does it supplant their previous identity? Would he be Raven Watcher, Aspect of Odin, or would the Sin-Eater just call him Odin?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a component whose space depends on how much of an identity the geist purported to have to begin with, which is highly variable. Namewise I should like to point out that the sample krewe's third Aspect is only called a future incarnation of its founder and also that deciding whether or not to call a geist by the name of its Aspect is down to how much a given individual feels the geist speaks for the Aspect.<br /> <br /> If you're familiar with Exalted, it's a bit like sorting out whether Ligier speaks for Malfeas in all the things he does or if his occasional disagreements with the other parts of the fallen Primordial King are separate from the workings of Malfeas himself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does a Sin-Eater know their Geists &quot;name&quot; anywho? I'm gonna go look in the book about that. </div> </div> </div>I'm of the opinion that geister's names as divorced from mythic Aspects are generally nicknames that stick rather than innate descriptors of nature like spirits have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T10:03:05-07:00","id":142442,"title":"","content":"This conversation is just reminding me that I really want to assemble a Geist group out of my pagan friends (I'm mostly atheist, but I went through a phase...). I feel like modern paganism, especially eclectic traditions thereof, basically gives people a really analogous model of how a lot of this is supposed to work, so it would be like starting with a group of people who already <i>get</i> the krewe channel and ceremony stuff (which seem to be the hardest for most people to fully grasp) on a really intuitive level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T12:02:26-07:00","id":143768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules?p=141288#post141288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For what it's worth, I think &quot;an aspect of archangel gabriel&quot; is an easier sell, if nothing else because it implies the Geist is a component rather than the whole, and that strikes me as more sensible than simply suggesting it's Odin or Gabriel themselves. It's a little thing, but it helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>This! <br /> <br /> Look at any modern day religion. You will find 3 groups: The ones who take everything to the extreme (and often become terrorists or at least outright hostile to people who do not share their beliefs - Think Al Quida) - the people who believe the religion but when confronted with proof will adjust their views (either by re-interpreting their religion or by re-interpreting the proof - think creationist scientists) and the big group - those that have a belief but are open to proof that they are in some ways at least partially wrong - think the majority of north american Christians.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna guess the majority of Sin-Eaters will fall into the third group, but the first two should still exist - either as sacrosanct, the anti-social group who like to insist that you're view of the metaverse is wrong, or whatever. The Geists - just like anything else - will go along with whatever the interpretation is cause they're not exactly on the forefront of moral, ethical or mental aptitude. They might go with it because it's the necessary lie, or because it's what they want their hosts to believe, or even simply because they themselves ligit believe it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}